Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/opencontainers/runc v1.5.3

H-3 of the runc series: newSetnsProcess refuses. Starting a process inside a
running container joins that container's namespaces, which the standard
library cannot do at clone and which upstream leaves to the C stage
(libcontainer/nsenter). A ze binary is built with cgo off and has no C stage,
so the call would hang on a protocol nobody speaks. It answers an error that
names the missing join instead.

The upstream body is kept, unchanged, under the name newSetnsProcessWithJoin,
which nothing calls. The patch that brings a namespace join restores it.

Needs runc-01-direct-init.patch: both change container_linux.go, and this
hunk's line numbers follow that patch.

No upstream pull request is opened for this change: upstream keeps its C
stage, and the change is specific to a build with cgo off. The design is
docs/architecture/container/runtime.md.

Delete this series when Ze no longer vendors the runtime.

